                        ],
                        "form": "darbârs"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "101992cd-41fd-32b5-9f86-c632f66811ea",
                        "entry_id": "76bf0013-e701-3245-837f-4321efb61abe",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Audience publique donnée par un souverain de l’Inde, y compris, à l’époque coloniale britannique, par le vice-roi des Indes. Le public convié fait généralement partie de la noblesse."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b12a47b1-4ff5-41eb-9c0d-d5ba6396b0bb",
                                "sense_id": "101992cd-41fd-32b5-9f86-c632f66811ea",
                                "text": "Le darbâr se clôt sur une note théâtrale : sir Pertab Singh s’avance, dépose avec panache son épée aux pieds de la reine et lui offre une ravissante broche ornée de perles qu’il prélève sur son propre turban."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f8ce6e39-2389-4bc8-afd6-c7f46b28b832",
                                "sense_id": "101992cd-41fd-32b5-9f86-c632f66811ea",
                                "text": "Au déjeuner, j’annonçai la nouvelle de la visite du roi à la famille. Chacun l’accueillit à sa manière caractéristique.\n- Ce sera sympathique, dit Mère. Je ferais bien de commencer à mettre au point des menus.\n- Il ne vient pas séjourner ici, Dieu merci, fit remarquer Larry.\n- Je sais, chéri, dit Mère, mais… euh… il y aura tout un tas de réceptions et autres festivités, j’imagine.\n- Je ne vois pas pourquoi, dit Larry.\n- Parce que c’est toujours comme ça, dit Mère. Lorsque nous étions en Inde, nous organisions toujours des fêtes pendant le darbâr."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a7e70166-34d2-439d-a7f6-4bcc1ee1ad4c",
                                "sense_id": "101992cd-41fd-32b5-9f86-c632f66811ea",
                                "text": "Lors de ce darbâr, Morgan le savait, George V avait annoncé des changements radicaux dans le système politique indien."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8241da67-ba75-4a03-b77b-2960d4c94039",
                                "sense_id": "101992cd-41fd-32b5-9f86-c632f66811ea",
                                "text": "Le transfert eut lieu en 1911, quand le jeune George V donna un darbâr – audience publique à la cour de tout souverain de l’Inde – auquel furent conviés tous les princes de la colonie par l’intermédiaire desquels l’empire devait continuer d’exercer sa souveraineté."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "51d6b509-6984-4054-ac41-0d5558bab10f",
                        "source_entry_id": "76bf0013-e701-3245-837f-4321efb61abe",
                        "source_sense_id": "101992cd-41fd-32b5-9f86-c632f66811ea",
                        "target_lang_word": "durbar",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "durbar",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "85bc0f33-2fcf-3a55-a5af-ad4fbaa580cd",
                                        "entry_id": "66d3bf1f-d37a-35fe-bca6-0f2dc2d087f3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A ceremonial gathering held by a ruler in India."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5fcb78d2-9656-4142-82f2-d3effc07252a",
                                                "sense_id": "85bc0f33-2fcf-3a55-a5af-ad4fbaa580cd",
                                                "text": "Sir Salar Jung was proceeding to the palace of the Nizam on his bocha, a sort of state palanquin, in order to be present at the customary Eed durbar... when two shots in rapid succession were fired."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d67b4b9d-b8c9-407c-b61b-f8b2be39cbc1",
                                                "sense_id": "85bc0f33-2fcf-3a55-a5af-ad4fbaa580cd",
                                                "text": "A month after his retirement he was summoned to a durbar in Rangoon, to receive the decoration that had been awarded to him by the Indian Government."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e93cb23f-f3bc-42b6-8b6b-bc3b87db6aa7",
                                                "sense_id": "85bc0f33-2fcf-3a55-a5af-ad4fbaa580cd",
                                                "text": "He decided to stage a durbar on the plains outside the city, at which the Afghans would be able to express their loyalty to their new ruler."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9dad0efd-a0d2-4813-ba2c-797429a617ff",
                                                "sense_id": "85bc0f33-2fcf-3a55-a5af-ad4fbaa580cd",
                                                "text": "Father had refused to see my brother privately and had chosen to speak to him at the durbar held to honour the victors of the Malwa campaign […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1d754b1e-07c1-333c-bd8c-b97ae10bd15d",
                                        "entry_id": "66d3bf1f-d37a-35fe-bca6-0f2dc2d087f3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An audience chamber."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ebbe5c8b-1e9a-42ad-babe-09f92dccace9",
                                                "sense_id": "1d754b1e-07c1-333c-bd8c-b97ae10bd15d",
                                                "text": "“If you cannot gueſs, perhaps the bird himſelf may inform you, Madam,” ſaid the ſultan, who was withdrawing to the grand durbar."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9e7f898d-999b-3deb-be54-022462be830b",
                                        "entry_id": "66d3bf1f-d37a-35fe-bca6-0f2dc2d087f3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The body of officials at a royal or princely court in India."
                                        ],
